{{also|Mun.|mún|mùn|mủn|müň}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|en}} {{m|non|man||must, will}}.<ref>{{R:Collins English Dictionary}}</ref>

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|sco|maun}}

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb}}

# {{label|en|dialect|Northern English|modal|_|auxiliary|defective}} [[must|Must]].
#* '''1894''', M E Francis, ''In a North Country Village''
#*: Ye '''mun''' ha' done wi' all that foolery &mdash; ye're gettin' a man now, an' ye mun give over that nonsense.

====References====
<references />

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|en}} {{m|non|muðr}}, {{m|non|munnr}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*munþaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*ment-}}; compare {{m|en|mouth}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|obsolete|dialect}} The [[mouth]], [[jaw]].
#* {{quote-book|year=1847|author=J O Halliwell|title=Dictionary of Archaic and Provincial words|publisher=|url=|isbn=|passage=A common cry at Coventry on Good Friday is: ''One a penny, two a penny, hot cross buns, / Butter them and sugar them and put them in your '''muns'''.''}}

===Etymology 3===
{{short for|mundane|lang=en}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|RPG|Internet slang}} The person who [[roleplay]]s a [[character]] in a [[role-playing game]], especially an [[online]] [[w:play-by-post role-playing game|play-by-post]] one.
#* {{quote-newsgroup|date=29 October 1997|author=
Jade [username]|title=Re: Male dragon in need of mate ^_^|url=http://groups.google.com/group/alt.fan.dragons/msg/ed55faee1dd02fbc?hl=en-GB&dmode=source|newsgroup=alt.fan.dragons|passage=Jade grabs a handful of brownies and nibbles on then,{{sic}} trying to keep her '''mun''' from reaching right to the screen to get some{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|date=4 November 1999|author=
Milelarau [username]|title=Re: Roleplaying|url=http://groups.google.com/group/alt.games.everquest/msg/3989433226d9f1f6?hl=en-GB&dmode=source|newsgroup=alt.games.everquest|passage=Wait a sec.... You mean.. this is a GAME??<br /> And here I thought that nine tae five job my '''mun''' goes to everyday was a game and Norrath was my home..}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|date=31 December 2001|author=
JamesStein|title=Sucessfully Powering Down a Campaign|url=http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.frp.dnd/msg/6c9c46057d8e07b4?hl=en-GB&dmode=source|newsgroup=rec.games.frp.dnd|passage=Any suggestions on how to successfully turn this into a good SL, which will bring the characters back into the range of normalcy, without leaving the '''muns''' feeling deprived of everything their characters earned?}}
#* {{seemoreCites|lang=en}}

